  "architecture_summary": "HTTPie is a command-line HTTP client written in Python. It provides an intuitive interface for making HTTP requests, similar to curl but with human-friendly defaults. The architecture consists of: (1) CLI layer for argument parsing, (2) HTTP client layer using requests library, (3) Output formatting layer with color/text UI support, (4) Plugin system for extensibility, (5) Session/cookie management, (6) Download/upload handling. As an HTTP client tool, there are no internal auth boundaries - it sends credentials to external servers as directed by user input.",
